0 -2.39999 TD
(ans =)Tj
T*
(     3)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
0 -3.75233 TD
(This command prints out entry 1 in the vector. Also notice that a new va\riable called )Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
0 -1.2 TD
(ans )Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
(has been created. Any time you perform an action that does not include a\n )Tj
T*
(assignment matlab will put the label )Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(ans)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
( on the result. )Tj
0 -2.55714 TD
(To simplify the creation of large vectors, you can define a vector by sp\ecifying the )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(first entry, an increment, and the last entry. Matlab will automatically\ figure out how )Tj
T*
(many entries you need and their values. For example, to create a vector \whose entries )Tj
T*
(are 0, 2, 4, 6, and 8, you can type in the following line: )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(>> 0:2:8)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(ans =)Tj
T*
(     0     2     4     6     8)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
0 -3.75233 TD
(Matlab also keeps track of the last result. In the previous example, a v\ariable "ans" is )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(created. To look at the transpose of the previous result, enter the foll\owing: )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(>> ans')Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(ans =)Tj
